# Allow-list for `vercel deploy` uploads.
#
# When this file exists, Vercel CLI uses it *instead of* .gitignore to decide
# what rides along in the deployment tarball — .gitignore is not consulted.
# So this file has to independently keep every sensitive/irrelevant path out,
# not just rely on git's rules.
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then un-ignore only what the build genuinely
# touches. Patterns are gitignore syntax, applied top to bottom — a later
# line overrides an earlier one, and un-ignoring a directory does not
# un-ignore files re-excluded by a later pattern.
#
# If a new top-level directory becomes part of the build (installCommand,
# buildCommand, or the api/index.ts function's imports), add a `!/<dir>`
# line for it here, or it will silently stop being deployed.

# 1. Ignore everything by default.
/*

# 2. Un-ignore the top-level paths the Vercel build actually needs:
#    - api/         the single serverless function (api/index.ts) and its
#                    includeFiles/import graph
#    - server/      TypeScript source that api/index.ts imports
#    - web/         Vite project: index.html, src/, public/ (built by
#                    `npm run build` into web/dist, vercel.json's
#                    outputDirectory)
#    - package.json, package-lock.json  installCommand ("npm install")
#    - vercel.json  read by the CLI itself before any of this applies
#    - tsconfig.json  read by the TypeScript/Node function build
#    - .nvmrc       records the Node version the app is written for
!/api
!/server
!/web
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/vercel.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/.nvmrc

# 3. Re-exclude things that live *inside* the un-ignored directories but
#    must never be uploaded.
# Local web env files (none should exist, but never risk it).
/web/.env*
# Vite's own build output — Vercel builds it fresh from source.
/web/dist
# No dependency should ever be uploaded from the local machine; Vercel
# installs its own via installCommand. Covers any nested node_modules too.
**/node_modules
# Private keys anywhere in the tree, EXCEPT the one Fleet API public key
# that must be served from web/public/.well-known/ (re-included below).
*.pem

# 4. Re-include the single .pem that has to be deployable.
!/web/public/.well-known/appspecific/com.tesla.3p.public-key.pem

# Everything else — .env*, secrets/, data/, docs/, mockups/, scripts/,
# tests/, README.md, site/ (superseded by web/public/, see README history),
# .claude/, .git — stays excluded by rule 1 with no un-ignore rule, on
# purpose. Do not add one without checking rule 5 in CLAUDE.md first.
